      "date": "1973-11-01",
      "kind": "planning decision",
      "description": "The R-4 corner property was occupied by a long-established non-conforming mortuary chapel, with about 50 feet of frontage on South Van Ness Avenue and about 100 feet on 22nd Street. By a 6-1 vote the City Planning Commission converted the mortuary's non-conforming status to a conditional use with no termination date, subject to conditions including street trees.",
